---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import DecorativeRings from '../../components/DecorativeRings.astro';
---
<Base title="India" description="The regulatory and legal situation for tobacco harm reduction products in India." wide={true}>
  <section class="breakout india-hero">
    <DecorativeRings class="india-rings" />
    <div class="breakout-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Tobacco harm reduction in India</p>
      <h1>A market larger than any other — and none of it regulated for harm reduction</h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">
        India has more tobacco users than any country outside China, split
        across smoking and smokeless products in a way most global tobacco
        policy doesn't account for. Here's where the numbers, the law and
        the litigation currently stand.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ground-section">
    <div class="ground-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">The bigger picture</p>
      <h2>A crisis being managed backwards</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="ground-grid">
      <div class="ground-block">
        <h3>The scale of it</h3>
        <p>
          India has more tobacco users than any country outside China —
          roughly <strong>100 million</strong> smokers and <strong>200 million</strong> smokeless
          tobacco (SLT) users. Nationally, <strong>9.3–10.4%</strong> of adults smoke, and SLT
          breaks down to smoking-only 7.23%, SLT-only 17.94%, dual use
          3.44% — not the single habit most tobacco policy assumes (<a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10263025/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GATS-2, 2016-17</a>).
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="ground-block">
        <h3>Bans that close the off-ramp</h3>
        <p>
          PECA, 2019 bans e-cigarettes outright — production, sale, import,
          advertisement. Nicotine pouches and snus have no lawful sale
          pathway either. Removing the lower-risk alternative doesn't make
          nicotine use disappear — it removes the off-ramp, pushing
          existing users toward an unregulated illicit market instead. <a href="/india/law">The
          law, in full →</a>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="ground-block">
        <h3>A government invested in the status quo</h3>
        <p>
          The state regulating this market isn't a neutral referee — it's
          a shareholder in it. LIC, SUUTI and other public-sector insurers
          together hold roughly 28% of India's largest cigarette maker (<a href="https://theprint.in/india/governance/govt-has-banned-vapes-but-owns-28-of-itc-indias-biggest-cigarette-maker/293547/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The
          Print, 2023</a>). A government profiting this directly from
          cigarette sales has little incentive to let a genuinely
          lower-risk competitor in.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="ground-block">
        <h3>Research and even discussion, restricted</h3>
        <p>
          In December 2023, the National Medical Commission directed
          doctors to secure Health Ministry approval before researching
          e-cigarettes or heated tobacco at all (<a href="https://www.tribuneindia.com/news/india/refrain-from-doing-research-on-e-cigarettes-obtain-prior-permission-from-ministry-nmc-to-doctors-572837" target="_blank" rel="noopener">The Tribune</a>). Even policy
          discussion hasn't been spared: a 2023 panel naming no products
          was branded "promotion" by the Health Ministry anyway.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="path-section">
    <h2>Five ways into this section</h2>
    <div class="path-grid">
      <a class="path-card path-green" href="/india/law">
        <Icon name="scale" />
        <h3>Current law</h3>
        <p>What PECA and related rules actually say today — for e-cigarettes, nicotine pouches, and NRT for contrast.</p>
        <span class="path-cta">Read the law →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="path-card path-rust" href="/litigation">
        <Icon name="document" />
        <h3>Litigation</h3>
        <p>The legal challenges to state and national bans AVI has organised and fought since 2017, and their outcomes.</p>
        <span class="path-cta">See the cases →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="path-card path-gold" href="/science">
        <Icon name="chart" />
        <h3>Evidence library</h3>
        <p>The published research behind AVI's position, including India-specific studies on smoking and SLT use.</p>
        <span class="path-cta">Browse the evidence →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="path-card path-green" href="/india/rti-replies">
        <Icon name="document" />
        <h3>RTI replies</h3>
        <p>What government research bodies and customs authorities told AVI, on the record, before the ban — organised by department.</p>
        <span class="path-cta">Read the replies →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="path-card path-rust" href="/submissions">
        <Icon name="megaphone" />
        <h3>Submissions to policymakers</h3>
        <p>Letters, rebuttals and calls to action AVI has sent directly to India's health ministry and Parliament.</p>
        <span class="path-cta">Read the submissions →</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .eyebrow {
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      color: var(--gold-dark);
      margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    }

    .india-hero {
      background: linear-gradient(rgba(18,19,15,0.8), rgba(18,19,15,0.92)), url('/images/backgrounds/green-hills-india.jpg');
      background-size: cover;
      background-position: center;
      color: #f4f1e6;
      padding: 4rem 0 3.5rem;
      position: relative;
      overflow: hidden;
    }
    .india-hero :global(.india-rings) {
      position: absolute;
      top: 50%;
      right: -10%;
      transform: translateY(-50%);
      width: 30rem;
      height: 30rem;
      max-width: 55vw;
      max-height: 55vw;
      color: var(--gold-light);
      opacity: 0.3;
    }
    .india-hero .eyebrow { color: var(--gold-light); }
    .india-hero h1 {
      color: #fff;
      font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 3.8vw, 2.7rem);
      max-width: 42rem;
      margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
      position: relative;
    }
    .hero-sub { color: #cdd6cf; max-width: 38rem; font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 0; position: relative; }

    .ground-section { max-width: var(--max-w-wide); margin: 0 auto; padding: 2.75rem 1.5rem 0; }
    .ground-intro { max-width: 40rem; margin: 0 auto 2.25rem; text-align: center; }
    .ground-intro h2 { margin: 0; font-size: 1.6rem; }
    .ground-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 2rem 2.5rem; }
    .ground-block h3 { margin: 0 0 0.6rem; font-size: 1.05rem; color: var(--accent-dark); }
    .ground-block p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.65; color: var(--ink); }
    .ground-block p a { color: var(--accent-dark); text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: var(--border); }
    @media (max-width: 780px) {
      .ground-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.75rem; }
    }

    .path-section { max-width: var(--max-w-wide); margin: 0 auto; padding: 3.5rem 1.5rem 4rem; }
    .path-section h2 { text-align: center; margin: 0 0 2.25rem; font-size: 1.5rem; }
    .path-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(15.5rem, 100%), 1fr)); gap: 1.75rem; }
    .path-card {
      display: block;
      background: #fff;
      border-radius: 6px;
      padding: 1.75rem 1.5rem;
      border-top: 4px solid;
      box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(20,25,20,0.06);
      text-decoration: none;
      color: inherit;
    }
    .path-card :global(svg) { width: 2rem; height: 2rem; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    .path-card h3 { margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1.15rem; }
    .path-card p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.92rem; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
    .path-cta { font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.9rem; }
    .path-green { border-color: var(--accent); }
    .path-green :global(svg) { color: var(--accent); }
    .path-green .path-cta { color: var(--accent-dark); }
    .path-gold { border-color: var(--gold); }
    .path-gold :global(svg) { color: var(--gold); }
    .path-gold .path-cta { color: var(--gold-dark); }
    .path-rust { border-color: var(--rust); }
    .path-rust :global(svg) { color: var(--rust); }
    .path-rust .path-cta { color: var(--rust-dark); }
    @media (max-width: 780px) {
      .path-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    }
  </style>
</Base>
